User-Player Interface for PawnsBoard

Key Functionalities
- Viewing the game state
    - Human players will see a graphical representation of the board and hand
    - AI players will receive the board and hand as a data structure such as a 2D array

 - Playing a card
    - Human/AI selects card from their hand
    - Human/AI chooses a position (row, column) on the board

 - Passing a card
    - If Human/AI cannot or chooses to play a card, they may pass their turn

 - Note: Human/AI will not be allowed to draw a card as it is automatically done at the
            beginning of their turn


Implementation Considerations
 - Design should support both GUI and text-based version of games
 - Interface only communicates valid actions without handling game rules directly

Example Flow
Human Player Turn
 1. Player shown their hand and current board state
 2. Player chooses to either play a card or pass
 3. If playing a card:
    - Select a card and board position
    - If valid, the card is placed and influence is applied
 4. If passing:
    - Game moves to next player's turn

AI Player Turn
 1. AI receives game state (board, hand, valid moves)
 2. AI chooses optimal move using strategy
 3. AI plays a card or passes
 4. Board updates and next turn begins
